no boundary was weakened, no new claim was introduced, and every remaining P### resolves to
a statement that carries the clause it is attached to.

MF1 — forbidden_behaviours[0]  (P010, P077) → (authored scope boundary)
      P010 is mechanism-first translation into a local implementation; P077 is not treating
      one's own learning history as proof. Neither is about WHO performs teaching, delivery,
      authoring, or marking. Boundary text unchanged, hedge complete.

MF2 — forbidden_behaviours[2]  (P128, P087) → (authored scope boundary)
      P128 governs WHAT to assess (plural competence dimensions, not one static score);
      P087 governs PACING to demonstrated readiness. Neither states an authority boundary on
      placement, grading, admission, promotion, or employment outcomes. Boundary text unchanged.

MF3 — handoff_rules[0]  (P010, P077) → (P010) on the supported clause + (authored scope boundary)
      Ownership of curriculum, materials, delivery, and marks is an authored authority
      allocation. P010 retained only on the clause it genuinely supports: the design reasoning
      is adapted through each principle's mechanism to the local learners, format, and
      institution. P077 dropped (silent on ownership).

ADVISORY (same defect class, fixed in the same pass as verify1 recommends)
      handoff_rules[1]  (P134, P128) → (authored scope boundary) + (P134) on the clause P134
